cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Knowledge or sparsity? Gene set masks in a single-cell VAE"
authors:
  - family-names: Miliarakis
    given-names: George
    email: contact@gmiliarakis.com
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
    city: Amsterdam
    country: NL
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3325-8386"
abstract: >-
  Code, result tables and figures of a study that asks whether the knowledge in gene sets, or only the
  sparsity they impose, explains how well a variational autoencoder with a gene set mask in its linear
  decoder captures the response of single cells to a stimulus. Six decoder variants (a vanilla model,
  the gene sets, three random masks and groups of co-expressed genes) are fit with 10 seeds on six
  benchmarks from two public data sets of stimulated blood cells.
keywords:
  - gene sets
  - masked decoder
  - variational autoencoder
  - single-cell RNA sequencing
  - interpretable models
  - negative controls
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gmiliarakis/knowledge-or-sparsity-sc-vae"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
